  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Which set is equivalent to $A={x\\in R:\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi x)=1}?$",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the solutions to the equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi x)=1\n$$\n\n are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\pi x & =2n\\pi  \\\\ x & =2n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $n\\in Z.$ \n\nSubstituting different values of $n,$ we see that the solutions are\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,\\pm 2,\\,\\pm 4,\\,\\pm 6,\\,\u2026\n$$\n\nTherefore, our set $A$ is equivalent to \n\n$$\nA={0,\\,\\pm 2,\\,\\pm 4,\\,\\pm 6,\\,\u2026}.\n$$",
